# Redis usage

Redis 7 serves four distinct purposes. Do not conflate their key namespaces:

| Namespace prefix | Purpose | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `cache:` | Generic cache | Always TTL'd, never treated as durable |
| `lock:` | Distributed locks | Used for shot-level regeneration races |
| `rl:` | Rate limiting | Per-tenant / per-endpoint |
| `idem:` | Idempotency keys | Keyed by the `Idempotency-Key` header; TTL ≥ max plausible client retry window |
| `progress:{job_id}` | Job progress for polling/SSE | Written by the graph after each checkpoint |

Every work-creating POST must check, then set, an idempotency key before starting any work
— check-then-set as one atomic operation, not two round trips.
